WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.267
-Thank you for being here. -Oh, my gosh, thank you!

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:05.534
-Sutton, you know, we were almost Broadway stars together.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:06.767
-Really? -Not really.

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:09.200
But you know what happened? I had an --

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.000
I got an audition for "Young Frankenstein,"

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.567
and you were in -- You were actually amazing.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:14.901
You were in that play.

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:16.200
-I was in the Broadway production, yes.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.400
-I was not. But I auditioned.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.467
It was the worst audition I've ever had in my lifetime.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:23.400
It was so embarrassing. I went to -- Susan Stroman?

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.868
-Yes, the director, choreographer.

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:28.267
-Amazing. She -- The audition was at her apartment.

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:29.634
-Oh. -In the city.

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:31.067
I think it was around this time.

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:33.200
It was November or October, November.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.167
And it was cold out. And I went in to it.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:37.234
I was ready -- And it's "Young Frankenstein."

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:39.834
So I go, "I'm going to sing..." She wants me to sing for her.

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:41.968
So I go, "I'll sing 'Puttin' on the Ritz.'"

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:43.501
[ Humming ] -Yep.

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:44.901
-So I go, "Yeah, I got this."

00:00:44.901 --> 00:00:46.667
So I go in, I go, "Hey, nice to meet you."

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.467
I go, "Yeah, so I'll do 'Puttin' on the..."

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:49.901
She goes, "'Puttin' on the Ritz'?

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:51.701
Everyone knows that one. I want you to do this new song."

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:52.734
-Oh, no. -And -- Yeah.

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:54.167
She goes, "Here's a pianist here.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:55.934
He'll walk you through it and you'll learn it.

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:57.634
I'll give you like ten minutes to learn it,

00:00:57.634 --> 00:00:59.167
and then I'll come listen to you."

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:01.033
And I go, "This is a nightmare."

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:04.400
No, it was the worst thing. So I'm looking and I go, "Okay."

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.767
And I'm looking at this song and I'm like, "Alright."

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:08.033
And I'm trying to learn it and I'm like,

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:09.868
"I can't believe it's not 'Puttin' on the Ritz.'"

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:11.434
-Oh, no!

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:12.701
-And so she comes back and goes, "Okay, let's try it."

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:14.868
I was like, "Okay. One, two, three."

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:17.000
I go -- [Off-key] ♪ Lightning, frightening ♪

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.167
♪ Lightning ♪

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:20.067
"Sorry, sorry. Let me do one more."

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:22.767
It was the worst. And I started to flop sweat.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:26.133
And I remember walking home, and steam was coming off me.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:28.667
That's how embarrassed I was. It was that embarrassing.

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.167
It was the worst. -I'm sorry.

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:31.567
-Yeah. No, it was fine.

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:32.934
Turns out the show was great,

00:01:32.934 --> 00:01:35.534
and obviously I wasn't the right part for that, but wow.

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:37.334
-Yeah. -It was --

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:39.801
I mean, I haven't heard from Susan since.

00:01:39.801 --> 00:01:41.434
-No. [ Laughs ] -And she's local.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.200
-That's a nightmare. Auditions are the worst.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.200
-Have you had a bad audition? -Um...

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.467
-Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:51.367
Of course. You're Sutton Foster!

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:53.234
Well, of course!

00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:55.067
Of course you wouldn't have a bad audition.

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:57.100
You're Sutton Foster. What am I talking about?

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.934
-Oh, that was -- Yeah, well.

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:02.868
-Can we talk about "Music Man"? -Sure! Yes!

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:05.667
-You haven't done a musical in eight years, and then you go --

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.567
This is the one you want to come back to?

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:09.167
I mean, this is a big role.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:11.701
-It was -- You know, I, um -- Yeah, I was --

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:13.734
There was something very exciting

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:18.634
about doing a classic musical starring opposite Hugh Jackman,

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:21.300
which was really, really exciting.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.901
And I -- When we were originally supposed to do it,

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:25.934
which was, like, three years ago, pre all of the COVID stuff.

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:28.033
-That's correct. That's right.

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:30.501
-I'm a mom now, so I have a 5-year-old daughter.

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:32.868
She just started kindergarten.

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:34.601
[ Applause ] -Oh, that's a big deal.

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:35.968
-Yeah, she's awesome. She's the best.

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:37.234
And so I was, like, really excited

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:39.334
to come back to Broadway and to be a mom.

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:42.133
And there was something very exciting about doing a show

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.868
like this because I thought, "Oh, this is a show

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:45.100
she could come see." -Yeah.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.167
-So she's seen it now, like, five times,

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:49.100
and she has lots of thoughts.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.400
-That's so cute. And how great is Hugh Jackman.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.767
Could he not be more of a gentleman?

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:54.968
-He's pretty fantastic.

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:56.601
I couldn't ask for a better leading man.

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:57.901
-Yeah. -He's pretty awesome.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:03:00.601
-I know that -- I've heard that backstage

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:02.267
when you're doing these types of things,

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:03.734
I know you FaceTime your daughter.

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:06.868
-Yeah, so, every show before that half hour,

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:09.601
30 minutes before the show, I FaceTime Emily.

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.400
And I have a whole stack of books.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.767
Because the hardest part is that our schedule --

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:16.100
my schedule is opposite of hers.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.133
So when she's -- I know it's hard.

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:19.767
I don't get to do all the "night-nights" and everything,

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:21.133
but I do read -- we read her --

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.534
I read her books from my dressing room.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:23.767
-Yeah.

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.434
-And she gets to watch me get ready for the show

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:27.868
and listens to the overture and everything.

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:30.200
-But, also, you crochet a lot. -I do. I'm a crocheter.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.200
I crochet in the -- I wrote a book about it.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.667
-Yes! Oh, I'm so prepared.

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:37.467
This is your book, "Hooked."

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:41.133
I mean -- But that's a great way to pass the time if you're --

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:42.934
-It is. So, when I'm not on stage,

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:45.701
I'm usually crocheting or making things, or, you know.

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:48.767
It's a pretty -- In fact, I actually made you something.

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.868
-I was really -- No, you did not.

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:52.167
-Of course. -I was actually going to ask you.

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:53.534
I go, "You know what? I'll do it next time."

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:55.567
You made me something? -So it's a --

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.133
-Oh, my gosh. I know what it --

00:03:57.133 --> 00:03:59.400
I know exactly what it is.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:03.734
-But it's -- it's handy

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:05.701
because it's also a toilet paper roll cover.

00:04:05.701 --> 00:04:07.100
-Yeah, it's... [ Laughs ]

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.067
You are the greatest, Sutton Foster.

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:11.200
-Toilet paper can be fun. -I cannot believe --

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.868
You are the best for doing this. I love that you do this.

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.400
Thank you so much for that.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.467
I was going to ask you, but I didn't want to impose.

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:18.868
-It was made in the dressing room, so...

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:20.267
-Yeah. Thank you very much.

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:22.934
And it will live in my dressing room.

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:24.634
Yeah, it will. -I'm so glad.

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:26.434
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:28.601
[ Applause ]

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.534
Before we go, I want to quickly mention,

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:33.234
you're very outspoken about how great your understudies are...

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:34.567
-Yes! -...on the show.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.734
And I just figured why not give them a shoutout here

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:38.400
if we can tonight on the show.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.367
Understudies, obviously, that's --

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:44.167
You know, if the star is sick or out or something

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:46.033
or if something happens, they have to come in.

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:47.400
-Yeah. -And you have a lot of that

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.000
happening on your show. -Of course we do.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.501
I mean, I feel like it's --

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:52.234
You know, we're living in a very unpredictable time.

00:04:52.234 --> 00:04:54.334
-Yeah. -But I am so proud

00:04:54.334 --> 00:04:56.000
of our company because every --

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.734
It is a company, no matter whether you are on stage

00:04:58.734 --> 00:05:00.334
every -- eight times a week

00:05:00.334 --> 00:05:03.334
or whether you are an understudy, a swing.

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:06.067
It is -- We are this team, and we --

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:08.467
Especially early on because we were --

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:11.868
We came back, you know, at the height of the pandemic.

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:15.934
And everyone has risen to the occasion.

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:18.334
We have -- We have kids in the show who are understudies.

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:20.767
We have a 10-year-old, Emily Hoder,

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:24.834
who at one point was covering three different roles at a time.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:27.534
The other night, we had a boy, Michael Cash,

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:29.601
went on for the first time as Winthrop.

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:33.234
Had been a huge "Greatest Showman" fan,

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:36.467
and I'm sitting there watching him play a scene

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:38.000
opposite Hugh Jackman, and I'm like...

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.868
[Sobbing] "I can't believe it!"

00:05:39.868 --> 00:05:42.367
He was just this little boy that was, like, a big fan,

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:43.601
and the next thing you know,

00:05:43.601 --> 00:05:45.133
he's starring opposite Hugh Jackman on Broadway.

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:46.400
-With Hugh Jackman on Broadway, yeah.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.300
-And it's just -- And, like, crushing it.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.634
-Yeah. -And so it's pretty awesome.

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.200
-And Sutton Foster, by the way. Hello.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:55.400
-Oh, yeah, I was there, too. -That's a big deal, yeah.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.100
Have a great rest of the run. -Thank you.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.567
-Thank you so much for this. Thank you for being here.

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:01.734
I love this so much. Sutton Foster, everyone.

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:03.200
Go see "The Music Man"

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.534
at the Winter Garden Theatre through January 1st.

00:06:05.534 --> 00:06:09.133
We'll be right back with Killer Mike. Stick around!

